x86_64-linux  clang emits __clang_call_terminate and the _ZSt9terminatev it calls - the helper that ends the program if a destructor throws while an exception is already unwinding. cxx1 runs destructors during unwinding - that is 6.4, and it landed - but emits no guard around them, so a destructor that throws while an exception is already unwinding ends the program by whatever the runtime does rather than through this helper
arm64-darwin  same
